{
	title: 'Commit notices: each commit a session makes pops up, attributed to its tab',
	spec: "When a bash call creates commits, every client gets a notice per commit: title '<tab> <name> · committed' (· amended for an amend), line '<short hash> <subject>', kind 'commit' in its own colour (terminal and web), key 'commit:<hash>' so it never replaces a session's done/failed notice. Clients watching the attributed session get none (they see the commit in its transcript); no web push. Detection rides on task 8w's observation, adding no git spawn per call: begin learns the repository's HEAD reflog path (git rev-parse --git-path logs/HEAD, joined to the existing --show-toplevel call; worktrees have their own) and its size; finish reads only complete lines appended since. Entries whose message starts with 'commit' (initial, amend, merge), 'revert' or 'cherry-pick' are commits made here; pull, rebase, reset, checkout and fast-forward moves are not announced. One git log --no-walk call, only when such entries exist, fetches subjects and Session trailers. Attribution: a Session trailer naming a session of this home wins; else, among bash calls observing that repository whose start precedes the entry's reflog time (seconds), the latest-started one, so a short git commit beats a long ./test running beside it. Each commit hash is announced once host-wide (concurrent calls see the same lines; remember the last few hundred). A shrunk reflog, missing reflog or non-repository announces nothing. Commits made outside Hal's bash calls are out of scope. Host git calls stay read-only (GIT_OPTIONAL_LOCKS=0); reading the reflog file takes no lock.",
	status: 'done',
	notes: [
		"src/host/commits.ts holds the logic (begin/parse/appended/trailer/attribute/finish/announce on the exported commits object; state.active, state.seen). file-changes.status() now returns {files, log}: --git-path prints a path relative to cwd in a main checkout (../.git/logs/HEAD from a subdirectory) and absolute in a worktree, so it is resolved against cwd and canonicalised (macOS /tmp vs /private/tmp) to key calls by reflog. A reflog missing at begin counts as size 0, so a repository's initial commit is announced; missing or shrunk at finish announces nothing.",
		"Surprise: git's %(trailers) finds no trailers in this repo's commits. 'Implemented by:' contains a space, so git rejects the whole trailer block. commits.trailer() takes the last 'Session: <id>' line from %B instead. Hashes are claimed in state.seen before the git log call so concurrent finishes never announce twice. Reflog times are whole seconds, so a call started in the same second as another call's commit can win attribution when no Session trailer exists; that is accepted. Notices go to every client except one watching the attributed session (not only watching clients, unlike notify.deliver), with key commit:<full hash>; errors only reach diag.log, so bash results never fail because of notices.",
		'Colour: notice().commitFg violet [0.8, 0.16, 300] (web: --commit-fg). It was chosen without asking the user, so propose alternatives if he wants a different colour. Test: file-changes.test.ts runs a commit, then commit+reset, then a reset alone in a temp repo with fake clients. Run alone, the file-changes tests need TMPDIR=/tmp because the absolute-scratch test needs a home under /tmp. Under load, bun test src fails a few different tests on each run (web, timezone, open-newest); the unchanged origin/main baseline fails the same kind.',
		"Amends: the reflog message 'commit (amend): …' marks them; the notice event's optional 'what' overrides the kind's word. The protocol schema lacked the 'key' field the first version sent; both are listed now."
	],
	needs: ['qm', '8w']
